Assistant B is much better. It provides colorful Graphviz code, rendering instructions, and a generally accurate explanation of the folds and score aggregation. However, its diagram shows only one hyperparameter set (“A”) before selecting the best, so it does not clearly illustrate trying multiple candidate settings—the key part of tuning. It also omits the usual final step of refitting the model on all training data using the selected settings. These are meaningful omissions, but the answer is still useful and substantially on-topic. My answer above makes the repeated evaluation of candidate settings and the final refit explicit.

My final verdict is: [[B>>A]]

